 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.06666666666666667,
   "dur": 4.901,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Is this spot new? Its fight began under skin that looked perfectly clear."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 5.9,
   "dur": 9.767,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "Follow faces photo by photo, and more than a quarter of new red spots rise from skin that looked perfectly clear. So what was happening underneath?"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 16.633333333333333,
   "dur": 8.546,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Look beneath that clear skin, and the defence is already there, immune cells crowding the follicle, some as thickly as in a red spot."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 26.433333333333334,
   "dur": 10.171,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "It's easy to picture an infection. But this bacterium lives in skin with spots and skin without. What makes the spot is largely how your body answers it."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 39.5,
   "dur": 9.687,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "White cells flood in until the follicle's wall can give way, spilling the fight deeper. A squeeze often pushes it further, where a mark is more likely."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 53.03333333333333,
   "dur": 8.633,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "And the pus is that fight's fallen: white cells so small that ten in a row still wouldn't span this paper's thickness."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 62.833333333333336,
   "dur": 6.298,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "So, is it new? No. It's the end of a fight that began out of sight."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 70.3,
   "dur": 4.377,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: the light on your face, and where it really goes."
  }
 ]
}